    "text": "By Ted Streuli ,\n1 days ago Oklahoma City’s Eviction Rate Has Doubled in a Decade. New Data Shows Who It’s Hitting Hardest. Oklahoma City’s eviction rate stood at about 6% a decade ago. It’s now 12%, more than double New York City’s rate, according to a new data set from the Eviction Lab at Princeton University compiled in partnership with Mental Health Association Oklahoma. The lab will now track Oklahoma City monthly. Read full article",
